# Build context exclusions.
#
# This file exists mainly to keep three things out of the image:
#
#   * `**/.env` — backend/.env holds the Supabase service-role key. Without this
#     rule a `docker build` from the repository root copies it into a layer, and
#     layers are readable by anyone who can pull the image. The app would then
#     also load it in preference to the platform's environment variables, because
#     `config/env.ts` calls `dotenv.config({ override: true })`.
#   * `0_never-push-this-dump-folder/` — the database schema and the original
#     development passwords.
#   * `frontend/.env` — Vite inlines `VITE_*` values at build time, so a stray
#     local file would bake `http://localhost:4000` into the shipped bundle.
#
# Ignoring node_modules and dist also keeps the build fast and the image small:
# both are produced inside the build stage from the lockfiles.

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

0_never-push-this-dump-folder/

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.log

**/.workbuddy-ai
**/.codebuddy
**/.tmp-verify
**/.vercel

.git
.gitignore
.github

docs
README.md
LICENSE
